WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.526 --> 00:00:20.219
The next morning Jean Valjean returned to the Gillenormand house.

2
00:00:21.139 --> 00:00:26.264
Marius and Cosette had invited him to live with them, but he had come for another reason.

3
00:00:26.284 --> 00:00:31.068
"We missed you at the wedding banquet," said Marius, coming into the parlor.

4
00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:33.201
"Will you have breakfast with us today?"

5
00:00:33.221 --> 00:00:36.963
"Monsieur, I have something to tell you," blurted out Valjean.

6
00:00:36.983 --> 00:00:39.104
"I'm a former convict."

7
00:00:39.744 --> 00:00:40.725
"What does this mean?"

8
00:00:41.145 --> 00:00:42.286
Marius looked puzzled.

9
00:00:42.306 --> 00:00:46.348
"It means I spent 19 years on a prison ship.

10
00:00:47.068 --> 00:00:50.670
I stole a loaf of bread and tried to escape from prison.

11
00:00:51.671 --> 00:00:54.973
Then I was sentenced to life in prison for another robbery.

12
00:00:55.813 --> 00:00:59.735
If anyone knew I was alive, there would be a warrant for my arrest."

13
00:01:01.388 --> 00:01:02.989
"But you're Cosette's father."

14
00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:05.810
Marius could not believe what he was hearing.

15
00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:11.312
"I've been like a father to Cosette, but I'm not her real father.

16
00:01:12.713 --> 00:01:18.035
My name is not Fauchelevent; I am Jean Valjean."

17
00:01:18.855 --> 00:01:22.817
Then Valjean told the whole history of his relationship with Cosette.

18
00:01:24.037 --> 00:01:27.158
A wave of shock and horror washed over Marius.

19
00:01:28.019 --> 00:01:29.479
"Why are you telling me all this?"

20
00:01:29.499 --> 00:01:31.240
"Out of honor.

21
00:01:31.908 --> 00:01:36.169
I could live under a false identity as long as I was protecting Cosette.

22
00:01:36.849 --> 00:01:39.710
But I can't continue to do it just for myself."

23
00:01:40.951 --> 00:01:42.051
Marius shook his head.

24
00:01:42.071 --> 00:01:43.871
"I still don't understand."

25
00:01:43.891 --> 00:01:48.673
"Imagine that one day the three of us are chatting and laughing in the park.

26
00:01:49.273 --> 00:01:52.254
Suddenly you hear a voice shout, ‘Jean Valjean!'

27
00:01:52.934 --> 00:01:55.715
And then the police spring out of nowhere and arrest me."

28
00:01:55.735 --> 00:01:59.556
"But no one knows you're alive," protested Marius.

29
00:02:00.732 --> 00:02:04.413
"I still must do this for myself, to clear my conscience."

30
00:02:05.773 --> 00:02:07.834
At that moment Cosette entered the room.

31
00:02:07.854 --> 00:02:10.995
"What are you two talking about—politics?

32
00:02:11.615 --> 00:02:13.636
Men are always talking about politics."

33
00:02:14.876 --> 00:02:19.357
"No, my love, not politics," said Marius, as Valjean looked sadly at Cosette.

34
00:02:19.377 --> 00:02:22.558
"Come, both of you, it's time for breakfast!"

35
00:02:22.958 --> 00:02:23.998
said Cosette gaily.

36
00:02:24.018 --> 00:02:26.019
"I'll wait for you in the dining room."

37
00:02:27.219 --> 00:02:30.705
After she had gone, Marius murmured, "Poor Cosette.

38
00:02:31.385 --> 00:02:34.987
When she finds out—" Valjean trembled at these words.

39
00:02:35.008 --> 00:02:36.989
"I beg you not to tell her.

40
00:02:37.589 --> 00:02:38.810
She would be horrified."

41
00:02:39.511 --> 00:02:43.453
Valjean sank into a chair and tears rolled down his cheeks.

42
00:02:44.754 --> 00:02:48.857
"I'll go away and never see her again, but please don't tell her."

43
00:02:50.318 --> 00:02:53.380
"I give you my word that I'll keep your secret," said Marius.

44
00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:57.162
"But you must do what you think is right regarding seeing her."

45
00:02:58.203 --> 00:02:59.164
Valjean sighed.

46
00:02:59.664 --> 00:03:02.186
"Oh, I don't think I could go without seeing her.

47
00:03:03.586 --> 00:03:05.267
Please allow me to come occasionally."

48
00:03:06.408 --> 00:03:10.650
So a routine was established, and Valjean visited Cosette every day.

49
00:03:11.531 --> 00:03:16.033
She was puzzled by his insistence on meeting in a basement room instead of the parlor.

50
00:03:16.914 --> 00:03:22.737
But Valjean reminded her that he'd always been odd, and this was just his latest eccentricity.

51
00:03:23.998 --> 00:03:28.652
In truth, he didn't think he was worthy of meeting her in the parlor.

52
00:03:28.712 --> 00:03:32.353
Marius always made sure to be out of the house whenever Valjean arrived.

53
00:03:33.493 --> 00:03:38.275
One day Marius and Cosette went to visit the garden at the Rue Plumet house.

54
00:03:39.375 --> 00:03:42.696
They spent a happy morning remembering their secret meetings.

55
00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:46.717
Later that day Cosette described their visit to Valjean.

56
00:03:46.737 --> 00:03:48.678
"How did you get there?"

57
00:03:49.018 --> 00:03:49.578
he asked.

58
00:03:49.598 --> 00:03:52.379
"We walked to the house and took a cab home."

59
00:03:53.439 --> 00:03:55.239
"Why don't you have a carriage of your own?

60
00:03:55.719 --> 00:03:57.420
You should enjoy being rich."

61
00:03:59.176 --> 00:04:01.217
"I don't know," replied Cosette.

62
00:04:01.757 --> 00:04:03.157
"We're happy with what we have."

63
00:04:04.338 --> 00:04:08.939
In reality Marius didn't want to spend any of the money that Valjean had given them.

64
00:04:09.939 --> 00:04:12.720
He was sure that Valjean must have obtained it illegally.

65
00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:16.701
Marius was determined to return the money to its rightful owner.

66
00:04:17.842 --> 00:04:21.563
Little by little, Marius cut Cosette off from Valjean.

67
00:04:22.123 --> 00:04:23.804
Cosette made no objections.

68
00:04:24.484 --> 00:04:29.617
Besides, she was so in love with her husband that she focused all her attention on him.

69
00:04:30.857 --> 00:04:34.218
As for Valjean, he began to grow ill and weak.

70
00:04:34.939 --> 00:04:37.519
By the summer he was rarely visiting Cosette.

71
00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:44.341
One day Marius received a letter from a man announcing that he knew a secret about Jean Valjean.

72
00:04:45.321 --> 00:04:49.702
Marius recognized the handwriting and the paper that smelled of tobacco.

73
00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:52.483
The letter was from Thenardier.

74
00:04:53.664 --> 00:04:55.104
Marius agreed to see him.

75
00:04:56.196 --> 00:05:02.439
"I'd like to live in America," announced Thenardier, "but I need a little money."

76
00:05:02.459 --> 00:05:05.660
"How does that concern me?"

77
00:05:06.661 --> 00:05:08.402
"I have a secret to tell you.

78
00:05:09.222 --> 00:05:13.644
Monsieur, your father-in-law is an assassin and a robber.

79
00:05:14.244 --> 00:05:17.126
He's really a former convict named Jean Valjean."

80
00:05:17.146 --> 00:05:21.948
"So? I already know that, and I also know who you are.

81
00:05:22.624 --> 00:05:28.327
You're a scoundrel and criminal, who goes by Jondrette or whatever name pleases you at the moment.

82
00:05:29.528 --> 00:05:34.671
As for your secret, I know more about it than you do because I've investigated Valjean myself.

83
00:05:35.431 --> 00:05:37.672
He robbed a rich factory owner named Madeleine.

84
00:05:38.733 --> 00:05:44.316
As for the murder, I was in the barricade when he killed a spy, a policeman named Javert."

85
00:05:45.396 --> 00:05:46.617
Thenardier shook his head.

86
00:05:46.637 --> 00:05:51.520
"Valjean is Madeleine; they are the same person.

87
00:05:52.596 --> 00:05:56.397
And he didn't kill Javert; the policeman committed suicide."

88
00:05:56.417 --> 00:06:02.739
"What?" "I knew you wouldn't believe me, so I brought these newspaper articles."

89
00:06:04.199 --> 00:06:07.780
Thenardier drew some papers from his pocket and spread them on the table.

90
00:06:08.741 --> 00:06:13.042
Marius studied the newspapers and a smile spread across his face.

91
00:06:14.102 --> 00:06:17.183
"So this unhappy man is really a wonderful man!

92
00:06:17.783 --> 00:06:19.183
And that fortune is his own!

93
00:06:19.864 --> 00:06:24.541
He didn't kill Javert; he spared the spy's life!"

94
00:06:24.561 --> 00:06:28.823
"No, he's still a murderer and a robber," insisted Thenardier.

95
00:06:28.843 --> 00:06:33.545
"During the uprising last June, I found myself in the sewers of Paris.

96
00:06:33.805 --> 00:06:35.166
Please, do not ask why.

97
00:06:36.026 --> 00:06:41.768
Imagine my surprise when I came upon Valjean with a corpse slung over his shoulder.

98
00:06:42.809 --> 00:06:48.071
I didn't recognize him at first, but it was obvious he'd killed this rich young man and was

99
00:06:48.111 --> 00:06:50.072
looking for a way to dispose of the body.

100
00:06:51.292 --> 00:06:53.873
I managed to cut off a piece of the dead man's coat."

101
00:06:54.554 --> 00:06:57.115
Thenardier pulled a piece of cloth from his pocket.

102
00:06:57.135 --> 00:06:59.176
"And here it is."

103
00:07:00.476 --> 00:07:02.037
Marius turned pale.

104
00:07:04.218 --> 00:07:08.640
He walked to a closet and removed a black coat with part of the hem missing.

105
00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:12.301
"I was that corpse, and here is the coat!"

106
00:07:13.082 --> 00:07:16.323
Marius took money from his pocket and flung it at Thenardier.

107
00:07:16.343 --> 00:07:18.144
"Get out of here!

108
00:07:18.944 --> 00:07:22.505
The only thing that keeps me from turning you over to the police is that I know what

109
00:07:22.525 --> 00:07:23.625
you did at Waterloo!"

110
00:07:24.706 --> 00:07:27.987
As soon as Thenardier was gone, Marius called for Cosette.

111
00:07:28.007 --> 00:07:30.867
"We must go to your father at once.

112
00:07:31.528 --> 00:07:34.048
He was the man who saved my life at the barricade!"

113
00:07:35.249 --> 00:07:40.270
When they arrived at the apartment on the Rue de l'Homme Armé, Valjean was sitting in a chair.

114
00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:43.511
"Cosette!" he said weakly.

115
00:07:43.531 --> 00:07:45.212
"Is it really you?"

116
00:07:45.232 --> 00:07:49.341
"Father began Marius before he broke into tears.

117
00:07:50.801 --> 00:07:52.021
Valjean gazed at him.

118
00:07:52.041 --> 00:07:54.262
"Then you've forgiven me?"

119
00:07:55.522 --> 00:07:58.923
Marius nodded while Cosette reached for Valjean's hand.

120
00:07:58.943 --> 00:08:01.084
"How cold you are, Father."

121
00:08:02.124 --> 00:08:02.844
"I'm dying.

122
00:08:03.965 --> 00:08:09.486
I've written you a note explaining everything and leaving you my silver candlesticks."

123
00:08:10.466 --> 00:08:11.527
"You can't die!"

124
00:08:11.987 --> 00:08:12.767
cried Cosette.

125
00:08:12.787 --> 00:08:14.568
"You're too strong!"

126
00:08:14.928 --> 00:08:15.608
said Marius.

127
00:08:17.004 --> 00:08:19.345
But Valjean was growing weaker by the minute.

128
00:08:19.365 --> 00:08:23.268
"Come closer so that I can die happy.

129
00:08:24.108 --> 00:08:27.530
Let me put my hands on your beloved heads."

130
00:08:29.191 --> 00:08:35.474
He looked up toward heaven, and Cosette and Marius fell on their knees, overwhelmed with grief.

131
00:08:36.795 --> 00:08:45.100
Without doubt, an angel stood with outstretched wings, awaiting the soul of this virtuous man.
